      {
        "id": 253583,
        "name": "Amanda W. Reed",
        "username": "Amandareed",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/7ab992/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2023-08-13T01:50:40.906Z",
        "cooked": "<p>To vote for your favorite digital board games like Sentinels and Bottom of the 9th, you’ll need to follow these steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the BoardGameGeek website</li>\n<li>If you don’t have an account, create one by signing up. If you already have an account, log in.</li>\n<li>Navigate to the voting section or the page related to the top ten digital board game implementations vote.</li>\n<li>Look for the list of eligible games, and locate “Sentinels” and “Bottom of the 9th.”</li>\n<li>Cast your vote for each of these games by selecting them from the list or following the voting instructions provided on the website.</li>\n<li>Some voting processes might require you to rank your choices or give them a certain number of stars. Follow the instructions accordingly.</li>\n<li>After voting for your favorite games, make sure to submit your choices.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Remember to check the specific rules and guidelines for the voting process on the BGG website to ensure that your votes are counted correctly. Voting deadlines and other essential details may also be provided on the voting page.</p>\n<p>Good luck supporting your favorite digital board games!</p>",
